{# table; title: Fey.nvim; category: docs #}

Fey.nvim is a plugin for Neovim 0.11 and later that makes notes in the Fey markup language: headings that number themselves, lists, tables, dates
and planning, tasks, an agenda over all your notes, capture and refile, a clock, queries and databases, links between notes, and export. Everything
that has to be found across files is read from an index of your notes, so it is fast and nothing has to be open.

To read this documentation inside Neovim run `:Fey help`; the online version is at https://fey.github.io.


  I. Quick start

Install the plugin (see {@ link, installation.fey; desc: Installation @} for the other package managers) and set it up:

###  src lua
{
  'Loreite/fey.nvim',
  event = 'VeryLazy',
  config = function()
    require('fey').setup({
      fey_court_dir = '~/feyhollow',
      fey_default_notes_file = '~/feyhollow/agenda/inbox.fey', -- optional
    })
    -- Experimental LSP support
    vim.lsp.enable('fey')
  end,
}
###

Then:

-  `<Leader>;c` captures a note, `<Leader>;a` opens the agenda
-  `<Leader>;;` opens the navigator on the current file: the court, the hollows, the headings
-  `:FeyHollowInit` in a folder makes it a hollow, a folder of notes with an index

Nothing else is needed: the tree-sitter grammar is built the first time a Fey file is opened, and the index of a hollow is kept up to date in the
background.


  II. How the pieces fit

-  A **note** is a Fey file, `.fey`. Its headings have **signatures**, `I.`, `I.A.`, `II.`, that the plugin keeps in order when headings are moved,
   added or removed.
-  A **hollow** is a folder of notes with a `.fey` folder inside, that holds its **vault**: the index (a database of the headings, tags, dates, tasks,
   links, labels, source blocks and footnotes of every note of the hollow).
-  The **court** is the folder `fey_court_dir` that every hollow is registered in, with the agenda inbox and the settings of all your notes.
-  A **tag** is a piece of syntax that says something about the text around it: a date, a status, a link, a query. {@ link, tags.fey; desc: The reference of tags @} lists all of them.
-  The words of a heading are its **labels**.

The agenda, the queries, refile, the links and the exports read the vault, so they work on every hollow of the court, open or not.


